Subject: [PATCH 2/5] CP7 5,000 targets, phase B (prototype): real staged
 scenario units and real fabric/accessory needs

The staged job computes the scenario with real units instead of the stand-in:
HIST_PREP -> HIST_EVENTS x k (2,500 sales) -> HIST_VALIDATE -> HIST_ROWS x k
(<= 12,500 cells) -> HIST_STOCK x k -> BASE_ROWS x k (250) -> SUPPLY -> SCENARIO,
then the phase A units; FABRIC_PLAN and ANA_TARGETS call the real fabric plan/needs
and material needs. Each unit runs copies of the single path's statements in its
order; a capture that is not clean falls back to the single path's whole
function (exact, loud stop if over 8 s). Job bounds 5,000 targets and 500,000
history cells refuse in HIST_PREP; per-unit bounds lowered to 250 targets and
25,000 pairs. No product SQL changed. Prototype stays under tests.

f05-staged-scenario (3 tests, local): 219 generated captures; 101 complete runs
byte-identical (analysis, text, Original, scenario, netting, matches,
allocation, fabric plan), 118 refusals equal in SQLSTATE and message (35
distinct, 10 unit kinds); intended cap differences and job bounds asserted;
11/11 mutants caught. With phase D: f05-staged-analysis 4/4, f05-staged-pages
2/2, f05-analysis-jobs 1/1, all four files together 10/10.

Known limit kept as found: with realistic horizons (about 60 KB of analysis per
target) the 5,000-target job stops loudly at ANA_TEXT (one text and sha256
over the whole analysis); the product move replaces whole-text units by pages.
Evidence (logs incl. failures, notes, benchmark JSON) for phases B and D under
docs/cp7/evidence/p19-staged/.

